From 372537380683749f8d5f921983e9af460e0d639a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 01:09:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Hades][Network] Projector control: the protocols of JVC,
 Sony and Epson, and what to ask of a projector

People with a home-cinema projector asked for Hades to set it by itself: the
lens memory by the shape of the film (constant image height on a 2.35:1 or
2.39:1 screen) and the picture mode by the kind of signal. This is the part
of it that does not use Kodi, so that a host test can run it:

- ProjectorLink: one talk with a projector over TCP, to the IP address the
  user gives (a literal: nothing is looked up), never listening. JVC D-ILA
  (TCP 20554: PJ_OK/PJREQ/PJACK, the network password plain or, for the
  models of 2024 on, as SHA-256 of the password and "JVCKWPJ"; INML and
  PMPM), Sony ADCP (TCP 53595: the SHA-256 challenge; pic_pos_sel and
  picture_mode), Sony SDCP (TCP 53484: the community; items 0x0066 and
  0x0002) and Epson ESC/VP.net (TCP 3629: the connect header with its
  password header; POPLP and CMODE). Written from the public descriptions
  of each protocol, read as data; no code is taken. Every step has a
  timeout and ends at once when Kodi stops; every byte is said in the log
  except the password and what is made of it.
- ProjectorPolicy: the class of a shape by the user's thresholds, with a
  band of 0.03 under each so that a picture at the edge does not move the
  lens back and forth; a new class taken once it lasted 2 s at the start of
  a video, then the user's hold (IMAX scenes, bars of a dark scene or of a
  fade move nothing for less); the memory of narrower pictures when the
  video ended 3 s ago (a playlist goes on in between); the kind of signal
  (Dolby Vision sent as HDR10 to a projector without it stays Dolby Vision,
  so that a mode without the projector's own tone mapping can be chosen for
  it), taken once it lasted 3 s, once a change.
- ProjectorFeed: what the renderer and the window system tell the control,
  under a lock of its own. The shape is no new detector: it is the bar
  under the picture that subtitles in the black bars already has (level 5
  of Dolby Vision, or the pictures measured), on the frame as Kodi shows it.
